From e71561f4c5d6bd756fcb54595142931a9ffeb3f6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jack Zampolin <jack.zampolin@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 16:54:26 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] test(membership): a crash never reaches a member whose new
 home never heard of the crashed member (fails)

The scenario TLC finds on MembershipSys (LiveCompleteAll and LiveConverged violated), run on the real hub and member
machines over the membership test world. Hub 1 is cut from hub 2 and hub 2 from member 4; member 3 homes on hub 1 and
lists member 4, then switches its home to hub 2 on the lower round trip at 100 s. Member 4 crashes at 130 s; hub 1
lets the lease go and reports it to its attached hubs and its homed members, neither of which reaches member 3. Every
cut heals at 250 s. At 400 s member 3 still lists member 4 while neither hub does: a complete snapshot of the new
home starts the omission clock only for entries of that hub's own copy, and nothing recomputes a view member the new
home never listed. The two control runs (no hub cut, no home switch) pass.
---
 tests/Cargo.toml               |   4 ++
 tests/membership_stale_view.rs | 127 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 131 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 tests/membership_stale_view.rs

diff --git a/tests/Cargo.toml b/tests/Cargo.toml
index 8e7e459..da83493 100644
--- a/tests/Cargo.toml
+++ b/tests/Cargo.toml
@@ -226,6 +226,10 @@ path = "membership_s13.rs"
 name = "membership_incarnation"
 path = "membership_incarnation.rs"
 
+[[test]]
+name = "membership_stale_view"
